{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387749-storytelling-kiths-of-arcadia-advice-and-experiences","id":1387749,"title":"Storytelling Kiths of Arcadia: Advice and Experiences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T10:01:20-07:00","id":1387749,"title":"Storytelling Kiths of Arcadia: Advice and Experiences","content":"This is a general thread for discussing player and storyteller experiences with Kiths of Arcadia or getting advice and feedback.<br /> <br /> I recently started running a game set in North Carolina, where one of the players is an Imp music 'agent' from Nashville who after his Fosterage was sent to the Carolinas to make his mark.<br /> <br /> As a result, I started writing up a body of backstory and fluff rationalization for how Imps &quot;work,&quot; not only with Kithain society at large but with each other.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Imps do not care about Freeholds as much as they care about accumulating 'cults' of Dreamers; part of the rationale is that an Imp in Bedlam is a BAD THING. As a result, when the Accordance War occurred, they suffered relatively less compared to other Kithain, but they still exist on the fringes of society due to not integrating as well to the new hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Imps do not care too much for the feudal hierarchy, other than &quot;counties&quot; make the cleanest divison of turf for who gets to collect The Devil's Toll from Dreamers and where from. Imps are roughly willing to negotiate with each other 'independently', regardless of Kingdom or Ducal lines, while Counties with Baronial usurpations or without a ruling Count are &quot;great for business,&quot; since the breakdown of law and order makes business very good.<br /> <br /> Because Imps can see into each other's soul yet each have to mutually resist compulsion to haggle with one another, face-to-face meetings are a rarity unless there is a massive power difference between one of the two Imps. Rather, they will coordinate through a series of intermediaries, couriers, and catspaws.<br /> <br /> Imps tend to range the gamut of affectations and styles. On one hand, you have your &quot;pitchfork and horns&quot; minions, your Suit and Tie Southern Dandy devils, your psychotic anime bishonen Imps, your classic &quot;Harvester of Glamour&quot; death angel imps, or your &quot;Paganism through a Christian Lens&quot; tempters of sin. I have not created analogues of the Houses/Factions of Demon: the Fallen yet, as they are not Demons but the collective idea of Demons. However, I *might* have some movements within Imp society.<br /> <br /> The player is currently assigned a new &quot;turf&quot; in the wake of his predecessor's suspicous demise, and will be interacting with the other players on a frequent basis. Currently, travelling to his new territory has required its own mix of negotiation with several turf bosses, and some favors...and he currently is in a teleconference with one particular boss, Xaphan Hellforge, who has a Tattletale videoconferencing system built from Imbuing a pair of Foxxconn tablet prototypes with Tattletale after meditating on the dark glamour of Orwellian surveillance and child labor...he's a lovely fellow.<br /> <br /> Let me know how you are using or have seen the Arcadia Kiths used in your or other games!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","user":"MagicJuggler","date":". 05-13-2020, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:17:13-07:00","id":1387892,"title":"","content":"I personally haven't gotten a chance to use any of the Kiths of Arcadia in my own chronicles but I'm also definitely really interested to see what thoughts and ideas other people have had about using them.<br /> <br /> Personally I've done a little with thinking about placing them in my settings for worldbuilding but haven't yet had a chance to do more for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:23:25-07:00","id":1387893,"title":"","content":"There's one missing element that's preventing me from using this book to its fullest potential: I have no idea what the original context was like. I vaguely recall something about a card game built around the premise of some sort of struggle taking place in Arcadia; but that's all I know about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T21:51:06-07:00","id":1387901,"title":"","content":"I treat Dragonkin has having &quot;noble by default&quot; like sidhe because the idea of &quot;common&quot; Dragons seems off to me. There are non who aren't at least considered squires.. they still have to buy the background as pcs but its a required purchace like Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:31:49-07:00","id":1387944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387749-storytelling-kiths-of-arcadia-advice-and-experiences?p=1387901#post1387901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I treat Dragonkin has having &quot;noble by default&quot; like sidhe because the idea of &quot;common&quot; Dragons seems off to me. There are non who aren't at least considered squires.. they still have to buy the background as pcs but its a required purchace like Sidhe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, in general I'm more willing to have Kiths besides Sidhe and Oba be Nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T20:23:47-07:00","id":1392113,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, another player opted to go for a Dragonkin who is essentially the Living Legend of Blackbeard. His mien burns with chimerical fuses and hellfire, and has currently been shipwrecked near the Shackleford Banks next to the accursed ruins of Diamond City, North Carolina. His &quot;hoard&quot; as he builds it will be more piratical. <br /> <br /> My main challenge will be treating the Dragonkin as more than scaly Clurichaun, especially since there are already two in the server.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T21:43:13-07:00","id":1392753,"title":"","content":"May I ask what kind of server this is being played on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna",